CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ copy calls the target: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^\[std::__1::__function::__value_func<.*\] assertion: FAILURE$
^\[~__value_func\..*: FAILURE$
--
The this-adjusting thunk of a virtual function whose parameter has no name
forwarded a variable its parameter had been renamed away from: the thunk's
parameters had identifiers but no base names, and converting the thunk
renamed them to `#anon_arg'.  The clone of a copied std::function was
placed at a nondeterministic address, and calling the copy failed with
bad_function_call.
